<dl class="space-y-4">
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Errors</dt><dd>Likely accessibility problems. Identify the triggering element, why the rule matters, and the appropriate correction.</dd></div>
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Contrast Errors</dt><dd>Measured contrast findings. Revisit Module 02: inspect the foreground, background, text size, and required ratio.</dd></div>
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Alerts</dt><dd>Items needing judgment. Alert does not mean failure.</dd></div>
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Features</dt><dd>Detected accessibility features. Feature does not mean “passed.” Inspect whether each feature helps in context.</dd></div>
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Structure</dt><dd>Inspect headings, landmarks, lists, and reading order. Connect these to the semantic structure from Module 05.</dd></div>
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">ARIA</dt><dd>Inspect exposed roles and properties. Their presence does not establish correct interaction.</dd></div>
</dl>
<p>In Details, select a finding to locate its icon and affected element. Use Reference for the explanation, then Code to inspect the underlying markup. Follow: icon → element → explanation → markup. Panel placement can vary by WAVE version.</p>
